n the case of the binomial</article-title><source>Biometrika</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>404</fpage><lpage>413</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040098-b015"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newcombe</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Two-sided confidence intervals for the single proportion: Comparison of seven methods</article-title><source>Stat Med</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>857</fpage><lpage>872</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9595616</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040098-b016"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1984</year><article-title>Double-blind comparison of loperamide HCl and placebo in the treatment of acute diarrhea in children</article-title><source>Adv Ther</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>14</fpage><lpage>18</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040098-b017"><citation citation-type="journal"><year>1984</year><article-title>Loperamide in acute diarrhoea in childhood: Results of a double blind, placebo controlled multicentre clinical trial</article-title><collab>Diarrhoeal Diseases Study Group (UK).</collab><source>BMJ</source><comment>(Clinical Research Ed.)</comment><volume>289</volume><fpage>1263</fpage><lpage>1267</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6437509</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040098-b018"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chavarria</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Loria-Cortes</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Carrillo-Henchoz</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1984</year><article-title>Control of pediatric diarrhea</article-title><source>Adv Ther</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>119</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040098-b019"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cordier</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Mozziconacci</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Polonovski</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Indications for loperamide in acute infantile diarrhea. Randomized double-blind study</article-title><source>Ann Pediatr (Paris)</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>653</fpage><lpage>658</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3318636</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040098-b020"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ghisolfi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Baudoin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Charlet</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Olives</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghisolfi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Effects of loperamide on fecal electrolyte excretion in acute diarrhea in infants</article-title><source>Arch Fr Pediatr</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>483</fpage><lpage>487</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3426370</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040098-b021"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kassem</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Madkour</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Massoud</surname><given-names>BZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mehanna</surname><given-names>ZM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1983</year><article-title>Loperamide in acute childhood diarrhoea: A double blind controlled trial</article-title><source>J Diarrhoeal Dis Res</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>10</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6384353</pub-id></citatio